+# Activities
+
+Activities are the events that make up an account's timeline: cards being added, assigned, moved, closed, renamed, and commented on.
+
+## `GET /:account_slug/activities`
+
+Returns a paginated list of activities across the boards you have access to, newest first.
+
+__Query Parameters:__
+
+| Parameter | Description |
+|-----------|-------------|
+| `creator_ids[]` | Filter by the user ID(s) who performed the activity |
+| `board_ids[]` | Filter by board ID(s) |
+
+The following actions are included:
+
+| Action | Description |
+|--------|-------------|
+| `card_published` | A card was added |
+| `card_assigned` | A card was assigned to one or more users |
+| `card_unassigned` | A card was unassigned from one or more users |
+| `card_closed` | A card was moved to "Done" |
+| `card_reopened` | A card was reopened |
+| `card_postponed` | A card was moved to "Not Now" |
+| `card_auto_postponed` | A card was moved to "Not Now" due to inactivity |
+| `card_triaged` | A card was moved from "Maybe?" into a column |
+| `card_sent_back_to_triage` | A card was moved back to "Maybe?" |
+| `card_board_changed` | A card was moved to another board |
+| `card_title_changed` | A card was renamed |
+| `comment_created` | A comment was posted on a card |
+
+`description` is the plain-text summary of the activity shown in the timeline, such as `David assigned JZ to &quot;Layout is broken&quot;`.
+
+`eventable_type` is either `Card` or `Comment`, and `eventable` contains the matching [card](cards.md) or [comment](comments.md) representation.
+For card activities, `url` opens the card. For comment activities, it opens the card and jumps to the comment.
+
+`particulars` contains details specific to the action:
+
+| Action | Particulars |
+|--------|-------------|
+| `card_assigned`, `card_unassigned` | `assignee_ids` — the IDs of the affected users |
+| `card_board_changed` | `old_board`, `new_board` — the board names |
+| `card_title_changed` | `old_title`, `new_title` |
+| `card_triaged` | `column` — the name of the column |
+
+All other actions return an empty `particulars` object. Missing board, title, or column values are returned as empty strings.
+
